        "Helena's apartment occupies the top floor of a renovated red-brick building near the Green Quarter. The place was much smaller than he had imagined, and almost perversely neat. There aren’t any sweet family photos. There are no live flowers or plants. In a fruit bowl on the marble countertop in the kitchen, three pears were placed extremely deliberately, with the stems facing exactly the same direction.",
