        "Outside the house, the neighbor's dog barked twice, then fell silent.",
        "Aunt Lena folded her hands on the table. \"When your father got sick, he knew there was a group of people watching around him. Developers, investors. Men who thought grief and huge medical bills would make him desperate. He received phone calls, letters, and contracts that looked generous but were actually murderous.\"",
        "\"What does this have to do with Ethan?\"",
